Package: GsheetGenie
Title: Build Analytical Google Sheets from R
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Jesse", "Brandt", , "jesse.a.brandt@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Build external tables whose derived columns are live formulas
    rather than pre-computed values. Wrap a data frame with 'magic.table()' to
    get a recorded-computation table: a lazy 'dplyr::mutate()' records each tidy
    expression as column provenance instead of evaluating it. The first export
    backend translates those expressions to A1 spreadsheet-formula syntax and
    writes them to Google Sheets via 'googlesheets4'. Also ships eager helpers
    for data tables flanked by live-formula summary rows (sums, means, etc.).
    Focuses on formula-and-layout logic; no formatting or styling.
